    Build the parameter claim declaration rows on both sides
    
    The parameter claim message code is aligned with the shared proximity group
    code while the committed table index keeps its single-row shape; the folded row
    still fits the group message beside its pads. A new helper builds the record and
    column declarations of one claim from the same message and plan reader on both
    sides: it registers the folded message root, recomputes the record seeds from
    the table name and shape, and turns each record answer and each opened column
    into a relation row. A test proves a chain, builds the rows twice and checks
    they agree, and rejects swapped and tampered openings.
    
    partial progress

